# Flows, Phases & Definition of Done

## Critical user flows (must work end-to-end)

**A. Course purchase**  
Home → Learn → Course detail → Buy → Auth → Checkout → Payment verified → Enrollment → Learn + progress.

**B. Investment**  
Login → Trading Floor → Opportunity → Terms/Risk → Amount → Confirm → Wallet/Payment verified → Investment record → Portfolio tracks status → Settlement/ledger.

**C. Withdrawal**  
Dashboard → Wallet → Withdraw → Amount/method → Security check → Request → Admin approval → Process → Completed/Failed → Ledger updated.

**D. Volt Society**  
Projects → Volt Society → Join/waitlist → Membership record.

## Development phases (PDF)

1. Foundation — brand, public pages, auth, DB, admin base  
2. Forex Academy — catalogue, detail, checkout, enrollment, progress  
3. Wallet & Payments — gateway, ledger, deposits, verification  
4. Trading Floor — opportunities, investments, portfolio  
5. Projects — pages, roadmap, Volt Shop placeholder, Volt Society  
6. Security & Launch — tests, pen-test, compliance, backups, monitoring  

## Definition of Done

- Every public CTA works  
- Every protected route is authenticated  
- Payments verified server-side  
- Balances come from ledger logic  
- Admin can manage content  
- Critical flows are tested  

When implementing features, map work to the matching phase and DoD checklist. Do not ship “pretty UI” that breaks money, auth, or compliance rules.
